Intern’s responsibilities
Selected intern's day-to-day responsibilities include:

1. Represent Kraftisium on campus and drive student sign-ups + resume uploads.
2. Host or co-host short awareness sessions (in person or online) every week.
3. Grow and moderate a campus WhatsApp/Telegram group for Kraftisium users.
4. Share weekly progress (sign-ups, sessions held, blockers) with the Kraftisium team.
5. Identify 2–3 student clubs or placement coordinators to partner with during the internship.

Additional candidate preferences
1. Candidates pursuing Computer Science, IT, or related engineering / BCA / MCA preferred.
2. Active in college clubs, placement cell, or student communities preferred.
3. Comfortable creating short social posts / Canva creatives preferred.

Who can apply
Only those candidates can apply who:
1. are available for the work from home (part-time) internship
2. can start the internship within the next 30 days
3. are available for duration of 2 months
4. have relevant skills and interests
* Women wanting to start/restart their career can also apply.

